  "outOfScopeCommentTemplate": "Hii Team,\n\nSeller reimbursement team no longer handles any Fees reimbursement's process. We have already updated the same in our Seller Reimbursement Escalation wiki:\nhttps://w.amazon.com/bin/view/IN_Reimbursement_Escalation\n\nFor ES:\n\nEasy ship Fee related concerns and/or their Claw back related SAFE-T issues are out of Seller Reimbursement's scope. Please reach out to following CTI:\n\nC: Easy Ship\nT: Program Problem\nI: Weight Mismatch\nGroup: Amazon Easy Ship Program\n\nFor FBA/Seller Flex Fees issues:\n\nFor escalations, please reach out to the T4 Credit Ops team by using the CTI:\n\nC: Fulfillment By Amazon\nT: Shipping Claims\nI: Fees Escalations\n\nNote: Tickets have to be assigned only to this Group: T4 Credit Ops Project IN.",
  "wikiNotFollowedCommentTemplate": "Hi Team,\n\nThis SIM cannot be processed as the following mandatory details are missing or not provided as per the required template:\n\n{MISSING_FIELDS}\n\nAs per the standard operating procedure, all reimbursement SIMs must follow the prescribed format with complete details. This SIM is being resolved due to non-compliance with the template.\n\nKindly raise a NEW SIM using the below format:\n\n{SAMPLE_FORMAT}\n\nClaim window: {CLAIM_WINDOW_DAYS} days from {CLAIM_WINDOW_FROM}. Please raise the new SIM within this window to avoid claim denial.\n\nReference SIM: {TITLE}\n\nRefer to the Seller Reimbursement Escalation wiki: https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/IN_Reimbursement_Escalation\n\nThanks for your cooperation.",
  "efWikiNotFollowedCommentTemplate": "Hi,\n\nSIM request is submitted without following the wiki guidelines/including all mandatory details. This leads to delays and inefficiencies. To ensure prompt response:\n\nPlease review the reimbursement escalation requirements at: https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/IN_Reimbursement_Escalation\n\nPlease follow the template below and create a new SIM with all details:\n\n{ SIM Title}\n\n<Team Name> \"Escalation for SAFE-T Denied\" <MID>\n\n{SIM Body}\n\n1. MID*: (Mandatory for all teams)\n2. Order ID*: (Share only order ID related to the claims do not share claim IDs) (Mandatory for all teams)\nOrder ID format:\n[Enter order IDs line after line only without any commas or any other symbols]\n*Eg: Use below format only*\n402-XXXXXXX-XXXXXXX\n403-XXXXXXX-XXXXXXX\n404-XXXXXXX-XXXXXXX\n171-XXXXXXX-XXXXXXX\nReason code from dashboard *: (*Mandatory for AMs (SR and SVM SIMs not for SP SEED))\n\n(Use the SAFE-T claim Dashboard to understand the status and denial reason on the SAFE-T claims. Note: This query is applicable only for SAFE-T claims. Note: If you do not have access to the dashboard link, please request access via https://permissions.amazon.com/a/team/SR_SAFET_CLAIMS )\n\nEg: Format : CTR_POLICY_VIOLATION(mention no. of claims affected) , POLICY_DENIAL\nNote: no. of claims affected) (Please use comma for separating reason codes only and put affected claim numbers in (brackets) only. Put commas after brackets ended\n3. Yoda Dashboard attached? (Y/N): (Mandatorily attach Yoda Dashboard Result in .csv or .xlsx (Account Management/category/sales and other team apart from SP-SEED)\n4. First level deep dives done as per SR Escalation wiki?: (Y/N) If yes, explain what first level deep dives done*: (*Account Management/category/sales and other team apart from SP-SEED)\n\n(For SR SIMs and SVM SIMs only not SP SEED)\n\nWiki: https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/IN_Reimbursement_Escalation\n\n4. For CTR related denials, please attach Network abuse proof or buyer abuse SIM/ARM SIM*: (*Account Management/category/sales and other team apart from SP-SEED)\n\n5. Provide detailed comments on why escalation and reimbursement is required: (Do not copy paste seller seller's VOS only please do a first level deep dives and mention why escalation or reimbursement required) * (Mandatory for all)\n\nNext Steps for requester:\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________\nPlease raise a new valid SIM after following all steps in the concerned wiki.\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________\n\nEnsure all mandatory requirements listed in the wiki are included while filing an escalation SIM.\n\nThanks",
